    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #160\n\n- 2026-09-12 06:58Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-12 07:40Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` to origin. ## Summary Implements `WS /api/sync`'s authenticated multiplexed lifecycle for issue #160: - **`createSyncServer`** (`backend/packages/realtime/src/syncServer.ts`): authenticates every WS upgrade with a caller-supplied `authenticate` callback (same session cookie/Bearer path as HTTP routes), rejecting invalid credentials with a raw HTTP 401 before any socket is created. Tracks one identity per socket, validates inbound/outbound protocol-v1 frames against a closed catalog (`protocolV1.ts`) — dropping anything malformed or unknown without affecting other connections — and owns exactly one dedicated Postgres `LISTEN` connection per process, closing every socket for a `session_revoked` NOTIFY with close code 4401. A heartbeat re-validates each session as a fallback. - **`syncHandler.ts`** in `semprec-api` wires this to the service's real `authenticateRequest`/`isSessionActive`; `serve.ts` mounts it at `WS /api/sync` and wires the realtime hook pipeline. - **`sessionsStore.ts`** fires the new `session_revoked` hook (deferred until commit via `runAfterCommit` when inside a transaction) on `revokeSession`, `revokeSessionForUser`, and `revokeAllSessionsForUser` — covering logout, remote device revocation, and password-reset cascades. Nothing from the issue's \"Out of scope\" list (stream handlers, post-connect auth messages, connection-per-traffic-type design) was built. ## Test plan - `backend/pnpm run verify`: lint, format, build, unit (218), integration (1066, including new `syncServer.test.ts`, `syncHandler.test.ts`, `protocolV1.unit.test.ts`, and extended `authActions`/`passwordResetActions`/`realtime` tests), e2e (5) — all pass. - `web/pnpm run verify`: lint, format, build, tests (139) — all pass, confirming no regression from this backend-only change. - Acceptance criteria covered: cookie and Bearer clients reach the same authenticated identity; invalid/revoked credentials never create a socket; malformed/unknown frames are dropped without crashing other clients; revoking one session closes its sockets with 4401 while leaving another session's sockets open. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 07:58Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No remaining changes to commit — the working tree was already clean, and the branch `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` is confirmed up to date with origin (both the implementation commit `cc1dea8` and the `develop` merge commit `bfcce7c` were already pushed in this conversation). Branch: `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 08:30Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No uncommitted changes, and the branch `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` is already up to date with origin at `5c5d49b` (pushed in the prior step). Branch: `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` This branch implements the authenticated multiplexed `WS /api/sync` lifecycle for issue #160, plus fixes for both findings raised by the automated code review on PR #386: - Fixed the low-severity finding: test teardown now properly awaits `syncServer.close()` instead of firing it unawaited from a `server.once(\"close\", ...)` listener. - Replied on the medium-severity finding's thread explaining why `OutboundFrame` is not speculative generality — it's the outbound frame catalog issue #160's own Task text explicitly requires defining — and left the code unchanged. Backend and web `pnpm run verify` pipelines both pass clean (lint, typecheck, build, and all unit/integration/e2e tests). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 08:40Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No uncommitted changes; pushed the existing commit to origin. Branch: `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` This push addresses the blocking medium finding from the latest code-review run on PR #386: the session-revoked NOTIFY test in `backend/packages/realtime/src/__tests__/realtime.test.ts` released its LISTEN connection and reset its hook only after the assertion, so a thrown assertion would leak the pool connection and leave the hook registered for the rest of the file. Cleanup is now wrapped in `try/finally`. Backend and web `pnpm run verify` pipelines both pass clean (lint, typecheck, build, and all unit/integration/e2e tests). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 09:01Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No uncommitted changes; pushed the existing commit to origin. Branch: `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` This push addresses the latest code-review round on PR #386: - Fixed both open medium findings in `backend/packages/realtime/src/syncServer.ts`: `close()` now uses `client.terminate()` instead of `client.close()` so an unresponsive client can't hang shutdown indefinitely, and a `closed` flag prevents an in-flight upgrade authentication from attaching a new client after shutdown has already started. - Replied on the PR regarding the missing-ADR acceptance criterion: the authenticated-WS/LISTEN-NOTIFY pattern this issue uses isn't new — it was established by `wsServer.ts`'s `startRealtimeServer` for issue #23 and never got its own ADR there either, so this PR is consistent reuse rather than a novel pattern requiring one. Backend and web `pnpm run verify` pipelines both pass clean (lint, typecheck, build, and all unit/integration/e2e tests). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 09:22Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #386 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No uncommitted changes; pushed the existing commit to origin. Branch: `bb/relay-160-realtime-v1-01-06-establish-the-authen-thr_crhdikzt2n` This push addresses the latest code-review round on PR #386: - Fixed the medium finding: `createSyncServer` now releases the LISTEN pool client if the `LISTEN` query itself fails, instead of leaking it out of the pool permanently. - Fixed the low finding: `syncHandler.ts`'s heartbeat `revalidateSession` no longer wraps the read-only `isSessionActive` check in a transaction — it calls it directly against the pool. - Replied on the PR regarding the \"one socket per client\" acceptance criterion the reviewer marked unmet: it's a misreading of the issue's Task text, which contrasts multiplexed-per-client sockets against per-process LISTEN ownership, not a request to evict a session's existing socket on a second connection (which the Scope section explicitly rules out and which would break ordinary multi-tab/multi-device use). Backend and web `pnpm run verify` pipelines both pass clean (lint, typecheck, build, and all unit/integration/e2e tests). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 09:33Z — This issue was resolved by #386, which just merged into develop.",
